skibidi main
{
    🚽 a native call directly as a mewing/goon (do-while) condition, with the
    🚽 body ALSO reading from stdin. visitor.c's NODE_DO_WHILE_STATEMENT case
    🚽 pre-visits the condition once before the loop body ever runs; if that
    🚽 pre-visit executed slorp(n), it would steal the stdin line the body's
    🚽 own slorp(count) should have read first, shifting every value read
    🚽 afterward -- observable here because both the condition and the body
    🚽 consume stdin, unlike a condition that only reads a plain variable.
    rizz n = 0;
    rizz count = 0;
    mewing
    {
        count = slorp(count);
        yapping("count=%d", count);
    } goon (slorp(n) < 100);
    bussin 0;
}
